tion measured in tritium releases from FS-1 and FS-2 [15]. The most significant change in the gas sampling from FS-1 and FS-2 compared to FS-3 was the addition of He-3.5%H2 into capsule and thimble sweep gas downstream of the irradiation zone. Addition of hydrogen in FS-3 greatly increased the fraction of collected tritium in sweep gas compared to the total calculated generation. For example, FS-1 and FS-2 observed total tritium release measurements of less than 1% of expected generation [15]. However, the hydrogen addition in FS-3 could have altered the tritium chemical distribution through isotopic exchange reactions to produce HT. Therefore, the measurements of tritium chemical forms from the FS-3 sweep gas do not conclusively show the original tritium chemistry upon initial evolution from flibe or permeation into the thimble. The calculated tritium production rate from the MITR full-core model is plotted along with the release measurements in Figure 6. Reactor power was held constant at 5.5 MW throughout the experiment, except for a 3 hour downpower during the second day of the irradiation. The reactor was shut down after the 40-day run, and the three additional tritium release measurements were taken at zero- power.

